WEBVTT

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.030
Oh, Hakumei.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:38.610
I recommend avoiding that particular alleyway.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.790
It's the territory of a well-known pickpocket.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.080
This is a lawless area.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:52.550
This place, the Honey House, is home to artists and con men alike. You'll find all types of people!

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.800
The House's motto is "anything goes."

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.140
You picked one heck of a place to live.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:04.810
It sounds like a pretty bold move to organize a concert here, to be honest.

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:05.810
Well!

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:09.810
It just goes to show how many people want to hear me—

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:10.650
Konju!
It just goes to show how many people want to hear me—

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.440
Nobuki? What's wrong?

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:15.940
We've been had.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:22.200
What is this?

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.500
They keep pulling crap like this...

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.710
They've gone too far this time.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.830
Dammit! Those old-timers...

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:36.590
There are some who hate the very sight of newcomers like us.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.970
The veteran tenants of the kakushichiku floors.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:41.550
Kakushi...

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.470
The kakushichiku floors!

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.770
Honey House has eight floors altogether,

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:52.400
and since the old-timers live on the kaku, shi, and chiku floors,
thread
bamboo
leather

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.520
that's what they're called.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.230
Really?

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.610
I can't take it anymore!

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.410
Let's go take them down!

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.820
Yeah!

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:14.420
Oh, try your best not to inhale the smoke here. It's addictive.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.630
Yo. Got some business here, big guy?

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.850
You've got some nerve!

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.140
Oh, you must be here about that pile of scrap.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.730
We put a lot of work into making that mess, you know.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.770
Be sure to clean it all up, m'kay?

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.810
You bastards!

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:38.690
I know I've warned you more than a few times.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.450
Know your place.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.070
'Scuse me. Can I ask you something?

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.160
Can you bring your leader out here?

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.580
Are you a new recruit?

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.920
Just a visitor.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.090
Sorry.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:00.970
Our leader left his post for good some time ago.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.300
In that case, I'll ask you.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:11.560
Does "anything goes" also include fighting back against you guys?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.190
'Course it does.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.570
Anything means anything.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.150
Is that so?

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.820
Okay. Let's get out of here for now.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:31.580
That traveler might be trouble.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.330
Actually, wait just a second...

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.840
Is that the former leader?

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.340
That's right. He made a fortune in the liquor business.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:49.060
He wanted to have fun until the day he died,
so he surrounded himself with artists and outlaws.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:50.600
His name's Ukai.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.230
Fun until the day he died, huh? He had the right idea.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.100
He sounds like you.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.980
Did no one take his place?

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:03.950
Apparently someone did, but I've never seen him, let alone met him.

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:05.280
Weird.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.110
What was his name again?

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:12.370
I was hoping we could get him on our side,
but it doesn't sound like that's gonna happen.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:17.120
Leader or no leader, if those guys come back,
we must resist to the very end!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:22.050
We'll carry on with our work even if we have to fight them off all the while!

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.130
Huh? W-Wait...

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.140
Stop! Stop!

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.640
Konju!

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.890
Save me!

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:34.390
What's going on? Are they with the old-timers?

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:37.020
I dunno, but we've got to go after them either way!

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.230
Uh, right!

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:43.440
Head up top! If it <i>is</i> them, then they're taking her to the kakushichiku floors!

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.710
We're completely lost.

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:02.500
Hakumei-san. Mikochi-san.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:06.510
I've been searching for you. This way, please.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:09.090
You found Konju?

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:12.760
Mikochi! I haven't seen this guy before.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.980
Tell us. Who are you?

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:19.600
Ah, how rude of me.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.520
I should have introduced myself.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:31.030
I am Higaki, the second generation owner of Honey House. I am the Keeper of this place.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:36.200
There is something I would like to ask your help with—in confidence, please.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.960
Well, Miss Songstress.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.800
Sorry, but we need you to keep still a while.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:49.800
At least until those newcomers decide it's time to submit.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.800
They'll never suspect that we're down here.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.100
What the heck is this place, anyway?

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:01.440
Looks like some sort of wine cellar.
I guess he kept it under wraps all this time.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.650
Typical Ukai.

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:07.440
But wouldn't Higaki know about this place?

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.320
Even if he does,

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.620
he'll never try anything.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.460
For starters, taste this.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:28.710
We call it the Honey House Julep.
It was the drink my late friend Ukai loved best.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:33.720
Mint, honey, whiskey, water, and something else...

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:36.720
He didn't skimp on any of those.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:48.980
What is this? It's super-duper delicious!

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.990
It's still not quite right, though.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:58.950
Ukai's julep was... Well, in a word, it was magic.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:07.750
Every time a conflict arose between the residents,
Ukai would come mediate and bring along this drink.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:13.340
It was a magical antidote to any grievances the residents might have had.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.430
Mikochi-san.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:20.810
I've heard tell of your cooking skills.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:26.020
Please lend me a hand in perfecting the Honey House Julep.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:35.950
After much trial and error, I've recreated it,
but I just cannot figure out what else is missing.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.290
Let's go, Mikochi.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.410
We have to look for Konju.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:44.750
I'll do it.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:48.380
Wait... Are you serious, Mikochi?!

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.170
Yes.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:55.800
He's describing a drink so magical that it could calm this chaos. If I can make it, then I must.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:03.180
If you make this drink, we can save Konju, right?

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.140
I'm sure of it.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:09.650
Okay. I'll help.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.110
You have my gratitude.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.570
Now let us head to Ukai's hidden storehouse.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:27.080
Half a cup of mint. The mint you use must have had a fulfilling childhood.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:32.340
Two teaspoons of honey syrup. You must make the honey bees dizzy by placing a spinning wheel before them.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.840
Is this the recipe?

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.090
Ukai was a whimsical man.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:42.350
Did you follow this recipe to make what we drank earlier?

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:49.230
No. It's too sweet if I make it by the book, so I'm using half the amount of honey.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:52.610
That explains it.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.070
Is all the alcohol you have right here?

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:59.370
No. The rest of the spirits are in this room.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.250
Higaki.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:07.790
Tsumujimaru.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.460
What's wrong, Tsumuji?

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:15.050
We have to get the songstress upstairs soon.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:17.470
We've spotted the newcomers coming down this way.

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:22.600
Since we're down here, I thought we could grab a few bottles.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:25.350
Go on ahead.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:30.860
It's been a long, long time, Higaki.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.820
Hey. Tell me.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:41.240
What are you even doing here?
Have you finally run away from the light of day, too?

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:45.200
Cling to him if you like, but you are <i>never</i> going to be like Ukai.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.580
Hey.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.420
Stick up for yourself, Higaki.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:56.340
So you're working with these outsiders, huh?

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:02.640
I see. Interesting idea, Higaki.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:03.850
There he is!

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.430
I finally found you, you goddamn lizard!

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:10.850
Where's Konju?!

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:12.100
That hurts, ya know?!

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:13.690
Bring us Konju!

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.270
She isn't here anymore!

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.440
Then take us to her!

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:17.860
Shut up! Get off me!

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.110
Mikochi!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.580
Tsumujimaru...

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:38.590
Higaki! Listen well!

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:42.180
We're going to do what we want, when we want!

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:44.600
Just as we have 'til now, and just as we will forever!

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:48.350
Why? Because Ukai is long gone, that's why!

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:51.940
The lizard got away!

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:54.360
Doesn't matter! Just hurry and put out the fire!

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.240
Are you okay, Mikochi?

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:01.110
Yeah.

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:05.200
More importantly, I think I know the correct recipe.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.830
Really?

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:10.330
In this recipe, I think the amounts are correct.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:14.750
It's the ingredients that you've got wrong.
Probably the honey flavor.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.500
The honey?

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:20.510
Yes. Something less sweet than the honey you're using now,

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:25.430
with a flavor that blends better with the whiskey.

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:29.640
If I'm not mistaken, Ukai kept a bottle of honey wine.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:32.140
Ah, that has to be it!

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:33.480
Where is it?

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:37.150
I believe we'll find it in Ukai's room. However...

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:41.280
His room was on the outskirts of the Kaku floor.

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:43.400
All right, leave that to me!

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:44.820
Be careful, okay?

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:48.280
Um, I don't understand what you're talking about, but...

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:49.490
What about Konju?

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.330
Don't worry. We're going to save her.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:55.290
Let's go meet up with the others and storm the Kaku floor!

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.460
Yeah!

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:02.010
What's inside this one?

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:05.300
Chopped shiso leaves and Sakaeya's barley miso.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:11.100
Tastes amazing.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.020
Want another one?

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:24.240
Those newcomers are awfully quiet. I wonder if they gave up.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:26.160
They got spooked.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:31.540
They might live in the Honey House, but they've just been here one or two years. Practically babies!

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.580
You've got that—

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:37.170
Wh-What's that?!

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:39.210
Is that... a mushroom?

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:43.550
Mushrooms!

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:51.680
Those little brats. They've come to attack—

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:57.560
How's it going?

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:02.980
The first group broke through.
The guards are in complete confusion!

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:05.360
Looks like they're losing their minds, huh?

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:07.820
They probably didn't expect us to attack head on.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:12.330
Although we're newcomers,
we live in the lawless district.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.910
When we do things, we go all in!

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:19.460
Okay. Ready to go, Group 2?

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.340
Preparations ready!

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.340
It's all you!

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:27.090
Have a nice flight.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.010
Thanks.

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:30.340
Group 2!

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:32.220
Charge!

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:39.600
They're holding us at bay, huh...

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.860
Don't let 'em get close!

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:45.610
Anything you got to throw at 'em, throw it!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:50.240
These supplies don't come cheap. Dammit!

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.370
Ahh! I really splurged on that one!

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:59.250
Snipers! They're shooting smoke bombs!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.000
Watch out. Here they come!

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:02.880
It's smoky...

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:10.720
Nobuki!

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.180
Let's go!

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.850
Fall back! Retreat to the guard tower!

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:19.020
Tch, we're done.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.060
We're moving.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.400
Okay!

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.520
If I had to say...

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:28.240
It feels like you're giving me a guided tour of the Honey Lodge's secret spots.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.530
Glad you like it.

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:33.530
She seems okay over there.

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:37.580
I have to take this opportunity to find Ukai's room.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.960
Let's see, third block on the Kaku floor...

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:49.090
It's the one with an orange triangular roof, and a wooden window above the wooden door.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.760
This is going to take forever...

00:15:58.520 --> 00:15:59.810
Not here.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:01.190
Not here.
Not here.

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:02.310
Not here!
Not here.
Not here.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:03.100
Not—

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:03.810
You're not going to have any luck over there.
Not—

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:05.560
You're not going to have any luck over there.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:11.070
This is what you're looking for, right? Ukai's honey wine.

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:14.490
Yep! Thanks for your help, Tsumujimaru.

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.830
Heh. You could at least act a little scared.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:24.580
Higaki wants to use this to make Ukai's julep, right?

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.000
He said that it's a magic drink.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.420
Ha! What the hell is he talking about?

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.840
Anyway, I'll take it off your hands, okay?

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.300
Go ahead.

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:46.270
When they say "anything goes" in this place,
they really do mean <i>anything</i>.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:54.200
We've blocked the stairs and cut down the suspension bridge.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.570
This place is like an island fortress.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:02.620
The newcomers aren't getting up here anytime soon. How do you like that, huh?

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:04.830
By the way...

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:09.250
I'm getting rather hungry. What have you got to eat?

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:11.260
We didn't bring anything...

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:13.010
Hey, guys!

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:16.090
Look! It's the newcomers!

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:20.100
They're eating some really delicious-looking food!

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.650
You're really good at this, huh?

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:32.610
The old-timers came up with this way of getting around a long time ago.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:35.570
And I'm the oldest-timer there is.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.620
<i>Hey, Higaki.</i>

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:50.880
<i>The number of tenants here is going to start growing and growing.</i>

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:53.760
<i>Someday, when I'm dead and gone,</i>

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:57.930
<i>I'm going to leave this place in your hands.</i>

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:00.850
<i>What kind of place do you want to make it into?</i>

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.390
I...

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:04.850
Higaki!

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:07.940
I can see it! It's the guard tower!

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:13.030
Man, I'm hungry...

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:16.950
I wanna get this over with and have a drink at the pub.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:20.700
Um, may I ask a question?

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:26.460
What's the reason behind all this?
Do you all just want to stop the concert?

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:28.290
No, not really.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:30.250
Huh?! Then what is it?

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:32.630
It's because you guys ignore us.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:33.670
That's right!

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:36.300
Messing with you all keeps things interesting.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:37.220
Yep, yep.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:40.760
Who knew it would be this much fun, though?

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:43.010
Turns out those brats are pretty tough.

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:45.310
This is how the Honey House was meant to be.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:47.480
What a selfish bunch.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:50.770
Also, that outsider girl...

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:58.360
She'll definitely be able to get a certain straight-laced old man swept up in this horseplay.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:18:59.320
What?

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.910
Wh-What's that?!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.570
Something's outside...

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:05.990
Hakumei!

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:07.580
Ow...

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:10.710
Heya! You seem to be doing well, Konju.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.580
No better than you, though.

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:16.170
There's someone else.

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:20.380
You all cut down the suspension bridge.

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:22.840
You'd damn well better make sure you fix it.

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:24.010
The Keeper...

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:25.350
Higaki...

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:31.600
You and your hare-brained ideas, old man.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.810
And at this time of the night...

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:38.190
Well, I can't handle the light of day, right?

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:42.360
So? Did you do it?

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.830
Take a drink and see.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:59.170
No. This isn't Ukai's drink.

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:02.880
It was never this good!

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:06.720
A guest helped me improve it.

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:09.770
We also made a batch using his original recipe.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.890
But then I finally remembered.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.770
That swill was disgusting.

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:19.150
It reeked of alcohol, right?
And there was too much mint in it.

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:23.030
Honey wine alone tasted awful, too...

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:27.370
E-Excuse me...

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.490
Where's ours?

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:31.040
There's some downstairs!

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:33.040
Let's all drink together.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:36.290
It's about time you let me sing.

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:43.720
Newcomers! We give in! We lose!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:45.390
We'll give you back the songstress!

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:48.470
So please, leave some for us!

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:56.270
Okay, one more song... Here I go!

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:09.450
Good grief. Nothing's changed at Honey House from way back when.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:12.040
That isn't true.

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:14.710
The number of people that never knew Ukai is growing.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:18.630
Well, maybe it's not all that bad.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:21.550
As long as we remember him, that's enough.

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:24.970
What's this? You've grown up enough to get nostalgic?

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:28.140
Hey, you two!

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:32.640
Hakumei-san. Mikochi-san.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:35.060
We caused you so much trouble.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:36.980
Oh, don't worry about that.

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:41.110
Let me drink that and we'll call it even.

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:45.110
Be my guest. But I'm warning you:
it's pretty rough stuff.

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.030
Well?

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.160
It's...

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:54.500
See?

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:06.340
When I die, I'm leaving this place in your hands.

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:11.510
What kind of place do you want to make it, Higaki?

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:15.140
I think...

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:17.480
...anything is okay.

00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:21.020
Anything goes, huh? That sounds good.

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:24.860
This stuff is awful, Ukai!

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:35.370
When the breeze is pleasant, let's eat outside

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:43.170
The olives are fragrant this time of year

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:47.170
And in the plum-colored sky,

00:22:47.170 --> 00:22:51.140
the stars twinkle and shine

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:55.680
After we take in an easy breath,

00:22:55.680 --> 00:23:00.060
the banquet will begin!

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:03.650
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:23:03.650 --> 00:23:07.400
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:11.320
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:16.160
It's itching to dance with us

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:20.120
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:23:20.120 --> 00:23:24.090
How about something botanical with pepper in it?

00:23:24.090 --> 00:23:29.380
We could even catch the moon with our tiny hands

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:32.930
At least, that's how we're feeling
